---
/**
 * Terms of use.
 *
 * Deliberately thin. The GPL-3.0 licence in the repository is the operative legal document for the
 * software; this page exists so a visitor is not left guessing what the site is promising. Do not
 * add a company name, a postal address or a governing-law clause here — none has been decided, and
 * inventing one would be worse than having none.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { site, links } from '../data/site';

// Update by hand whenever the text below changes.
const updated = '5 August 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="Sidewire is GPL-3.0-licensed free software, provided as is. This page explains what this site does and does not promise."
>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main" class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <p class="prose-meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p>
        {site.name} is free and open-source software. The document that actually governs your use of
        it is the <a href={links.license} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GPL-3.0 licence</a> in the
        repository — this page only describes the site and sets expectations. Where the two differ,
        the licence wins.
      </p>

      <h2>The software</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          You may use, study, modify and redistribute {site.name} under the terms of the
          GPL-3.0 licence. If you redistribute it, or anything derived from it, you must make the
          corresponding source available under the same licence.
        </li>
        <li>
          It is provided <strong>“as is”, without warranty of any kind</strong>, and the authors are
          not liable for any claim or damages arising from it. That is the licence's language, and
          it is meant literally.
        </li>
        <li>
          {site.name} creates a virtual display and forwards keyboard and mouse input between
          machines. Use it only on machines you own or are authorised to use, and in line with the
          law where you are.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Pre-release status</h2>
      <p>
        There is no released build yet. Nothing on this site is a commitment that a feature exists
        today, that a particular platform will be supported, or that a release will arrive on any
        date. Anything described as “coming next” is work in progress and may change or be dropped.
        The <a href={links.docs} target="_blank" rel="noopener">project documentation</a> is the
        honest, current account of what works and what does not.
      </p>

      <h2>This site</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          It is informational. There are no accounts, no sign-ups, no payments and nothing to
          submit — see the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Links leave for third parties, chiefly the code host. Their terms and privacy policies
          apply once you follow one; we do not control them.
        </li>
        <li>
          The site is offered as is and may be changed, moved or taken down at any time.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Third-party components</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} builds on open-source components under their own licences, which are carried
        with the source. Redistributing a build means honouring those too.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may be updated as the project moves toward a release. The date at the top is the
        date of the last change, and the history of this file is public in the
        <a href={links.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener">repository</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
